 "result": "I created three files. I didn't modify any existing file. I could not build or run the image here because I can't execute commands, so everything was checked by reading the code.\n\n- `Dockerfile`: three stages. `web` runs `npm ci` and `npm run build`. `build` (the stage name `tools/push-update.sh` expects) compiles `cmd/app` with `CGO_ENABLED=0` and leaves it at `/out/app`. `runtime` is `debian:bookworm-slim` with `tini`, `par2`, `p7zip-full`, `curl`, `ca-certificates`, `tzdata` and `util-linux`, and runs `docker/entrypoint.sh`. It exposes 8264 and 58264 (TCP and UDP), and has a health check on `/api/version`.\n- `.dockerignore`: keeps `.env` (which can hold API keys), `config/`, databases, `secret.key` and `.git` out of the build context. `docs/` stays in, because the web build reads it.\n- `docker/entrypoint.sh`: the shell entrypoint. `internal/selfupdate` and its tests reference this path, but the file was missing from the repo. The script chooses between an installed update and the image's `/app/app`, using the same rules as the Go code. It also handles `PUID`/`PGID` (drops privileges via `setpriv`), `UMASK`, and the three-failed-starts fallback. I checked it against `entrypoint_test.go` and `entrypoint_umask_test.go` by reading, but I did not run those tests.\n\nChoices I made:\n- The default image tags are `golang:1.26`, `node:24-slim` and `debian:bookworm-slim`. I could not confirm these tags exist.\n- The `-full` variant, which bundles FlareSolverr, is not included.\n- I did not create a `docker-compose.yml`. The docs mention one, but you didn't ask for it.",
